# The Rust API. Server-side only — never prefix this NEXT_PUBLIC_, the browser
# must not learn the backend's address.
AGENTCOUNT_API_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Whether to show the "get each census report by email" form. `true` or unset.
#
# Unset, the form does not render at all. That is on purpose: a form that
# records nothing is worse than no form, because a reader believes they
# subscribed and finds out otherwise when the report never arrives.
#
# There is no URL to configure any more. The form posts to `/api/subscribe` on
# this origin, which calls the census API server-side, which writes a row —
# addresses are stored by this project, not by a hosted provider. A flag rather
# than a constant so that collecting addresses stays a deliberate act with a
# date on it, and so a preview deploy can be left inert.
#
# Switching it on needs a REDEPLOY: `/` reads this per request and `/reports`
# reads it at build time, so changing it without rebuilding shows the form on
# one page and not the other.
NEWSLETTER_ENABLED=
